:name: PPA-100
:description: Pick and place arm firmware on an emulated Cortex-M4

# Runs the SAME ELF the Makefile.arm build produces. Nothing is recompiled
# for the emulator and nothing is stubbed out for it: if it runs here it is
# the image that would be flashed.

using sysbus
$name?="ppa100"
mach create $name

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32f4.repl

$bin?=@build/arm/ppa100.elf

# The firmware's telemetry comes out of USART2 at 115200. Opening the
# analyzer on it is the only window into what the firmware is doing, which is
# exactly the situation on a real board with one serial port.
showAnalyzer usart2

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""

runMacro $reset

echo ""
echo "  loaded. 'start' to run, 'pause' to stop."
echo "  'cpu PC' shows where it is, 'sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x...' reads memory."
echo ""
